  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gloom-sh/gloomberb/zipball/v0.15.7",
  "body": "## Highlights\n\n- **Alerts reach you when the app is closed.** A price alert that triggers while no Gloom app is open now arrives by email with the symbol, the price and whether it is real-time or delayed. Re-arming an alert at the same target emails again. (#1264)\n- **Forms open in a central modal.** New watchlist, New portfolio, Set position, Add alert, plugin wizards and every confirm open in a centered dialog instead of the command bar, with `Tab` between fields and `Ctrl+S` or `Cmd+S` to submit. Broker profiles are managed in the Brokers pane. (#1226)\n- **Pick companies on day one.** A new account with an empty or untouched starter watchlist is asked \"Which companies do you follow?\", with search and a grid of company cards. (#1247)\n- **`RISK`, `EXEC` and `EK` are Pro in the terminal.** Free accounts see an upgrade wall; the free per-company pages on gloom.sh stay open. (#1272)\n- **Market data comes through Gloom Cloud.** Quotes, history, fundamentals, research, movers and heatmaps load from Gloom Cloud instead of provider code on your device. Signed-out delayed access still works. (#1274)\n\n## Also in this release\n\n- Linux installs with no `~/.gloomberb` use `~/.config/gloomberb`, `~/.local/share/gloomberb` and `~/.cache/gloomberb`. Existing installs and `GLOOMBERB_HOME` are unchanged. (#1278)\n- The news source column credits the publication that wrote the story. (#1277)\n- Install with `brew install --cask gloomberb`. (#1275)\n\n[Full diff](https://github.com/gloom-sh/gloomberb/compare/v0.15.6...v0.15.7)\n",
